Object.assign(catalog,{"siteDescription":"MeteoCompare — multi-model forecasts, convergence and local reliability.","subtitle":"Multi-model forecasts","weatherDashboard":"Multi-model forecasts","webHomeIntro":"One robust summary, raw model forecasts and their convergence in one place.","emptyTitle":"No cities yet","emptyBody":"Add a city to start comparing forecasts.","source":"Weather data: Open-Meteo · MeteoCompare synthesis.","agreementAt":"{time} · convergence {percent}% · {models}","agreementBandAria":"Model convergence band","agreementEvolutionAria":"Model convergence over time","agreementOverTime":"Convergence over time","minMaxAgreement":"Raw model range · color = convergence","disagreementIntro":"Overall convergence can hide disagreement in one variable. Here is the next 24 h in detail.","disagreementReading":"Green ≥ 80%, amber 50–79%, red < 50%. Each variable uses its own spread measure.","historicalConfidence":"Local historical reliability","agreementNotAccuracyBody":"It measures current proximity between model families. Local historical reliability is computed separately from past errors.","chart_confidence_band_desc":"The band shows the raw model range; color shows convergence after model-family balancing.","consensusEyebrow":"Multi-model summary","temporalSpread":"Model spread","rawValues":"Model values","modelHealthMonitorIntro":"Model status: latest run, delay, coverage and recent incidents.","modelHealthDetailedIntro":"Combines data actually received with the latest completed run published by Open-Meteo.","healthMetadataNote":"Delay is estimated from the latest completed run with a 20-minute tolerance. 24 h/7 d incidents are only those observed by this browser.","apiUsageTitle":"API usage","apiUsageIntro":"Requests actually sent by this browser.","apiBillingNote":"The provider may count several units for requests covering many variables or long periods.","apiGuardNote":"MeteoCompare groups and deduplicates requests. Private API keys must stay server-side.","dataIntegrityIntro":"Checks local data and detects duplicates or invalid entries (schema v{version}).","integrityRepairNote":"Repair migrates old formats and removes only invalid, orphaned or duplicate entries.","storageMethodNote":"Sizes are browser estimates and may differ from actual disk usage.","analyticsCnilNote":"CNIL framework: consent exemption depends on the actual audience-measurement setup and whether it meets the applicable criteria.","analyticsPurposeDetail":"These statistics are used only to measure site usage, size hosting and track PWA installations.","analyticsEventsDetail":"Measured: page categories, external source reduced to its domain, UTM source/medium/campaign, general technical context and feature interactions (city search/add, views, comparisons, marine, export, sharing, refresh and PWA installation). No city name, coordinates, search query or weather value is sent.","pwaInstallFirefoxWindows":"In Firefox for Windows, use the web-app button in the address bar.","pwaInstallFirefoxDesktop":"Firefox does not always offer PWA installation. Use Chrome or Edge to install it as an app, or keep the site bookmarked.","privacyEraseBody":"Deletes MeteoCompare favorites, settings, caches, history and PWA components. This cannot be undone; the PWA cache may be recreated on a later visit.","webPrivacyBody":"Preferences and history stay in this browser. Only required weather requests are sent to the services used.","privacyLocalBody":"Favorites, settings, caches and history stay on this device. No account required.","privacyNetworkBody":"Searches and forecasts are requested from Open-Meteo. Favorites and history are not sent.","privacyTrackingBody":"No ads or profiling. If audience measurement is enabled, it stays aggregated and contains no weather or city data.","marineIntro":"Optional marine forecasts for cities near the coast.","marineTidesIntro":"Forecast sea-level evolution; high and low waters are approximate hourly extrema.","marineTideDatumNote":"Level is relative to global mean sea level (MSL), not chart datum. Do not use for navigation.","marineDisclaimer":"Indicative data only, not suitable for coastal navigation. Use official nautical sources.","biasMethodNote":"Local index based on D+1 forecasts compared with ERA5. It is neither an accuracy probability nor a weather-warning indicator.","biasReadingText":"Bias shows the average error direction. Absolute error, variability and trend complete the picture.","localReliabilityIntro":"D+1 reliability estimated from local history. Open a model for details.","multiModelReferenceDesc":"Comparison reference computed on the same dates for available models.","multiModelAverage":"Multi-model reference","webDetailedDesc":"Raw values by model. Missing data stays empty.","forecast_evolution_subtitle":"Compared with forecasts saved 24, 48 and 72 h earlier","evolutionTimelineHint":"Each row shows how the central forecast changed from H−72, H−48, H−24 to now.","settingsIntro":"Customize display, synthesis and models.","settingsInterfaceIntro":"Language, theme and density.","settingsForecastIntro":"Refresh and synthesis weighting.","webRefreshDesc":"How long cached data is considered fresh. Manual refresh always forces a new request.","localWeightedConsensusIntro":"Slightly adjusts the synthesis and convergence using past local reliability.","localWeightedConsensusNote":"Weights stay within 0.75×–1.25×. Raw model values never change.","historyRefreshIntro":"Builds local reliability from past D+1 forecasts and ERA5. One initialization per city is enough.","historyAdvice":"History then grows automatically. Run again only to rebuild it.","forecastModelSettingsDesc":"Choose the models to compare. Changes apply on the next refresh.","localDataIntro":"Review, back up or erase data stored in this browser.","storageBreakdownIntro":"Simple view of stored data.","storageByCityIntro":"Storage split by city.","storageTechnicalIntro":"Browser storage details.","storageAdvancedIntro":"By city, integrity, API and technical storage.","backupIntro":"Export favorites and settings, with any history or caches you choose.","aboutLead":"MeteoCompare combines several models into a robust summary without hiding their differences.","aboutMethodLead":"Raw values stay unchanged; the synthesis balances model families and limits outlier influence.","aboutStepModelsBody":"Loads the models available for the city.","aboutStepCompareBody":"Aligns matching forecast times and keeps missing data missing.","aboutStepReadBody":"Combines weighted medians, rain probability and scenarios into a central forecast.","aboutAgreementBody":"Two separate signals: current convergence and local historical reliability.","aboutConvergenceBody":"Measures how close forecasts are across model families.","aboutHistoryBody":"Summarizes past local performance when enough history exists. It is not an accuracy probability.","aboutRawBody":"Every model remains visible unchanged so disagreements can be inspected.","aboutDataBody":"Forecasts via Open-Meteo. Favorites, settings, caches and history stay local. No ads or profiling.","aboutMarineBody":"Coastal mode adds waves, swell, sea temperature and sea level when a nearby marine grid is available.","aboutInstallBody":"Install the PWA or use the Android app.","pwaBody":"Installs the site as an app and keeps a local cache.","androidBody":"Android app available on Google Play.","supportBodyDetailed":"MeteoCompare is free, open source, ad-free and does not profile users. You can support development and new model integrations."});
